module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.discriminating_evidence_authored_into_the_operational_population

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data discriminating_evidence_authored_into_the_operational_population: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "discriminating_evidence_authored_into_the_operational_population" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a check's discriminating RED is authored as rows in the LIVE SUBJECT LIST the check reads** (the probe is genuine, the arm it exercises is genuine, and the expected verdict is a refusal -- so every ordinary run of the instrument refuses about one of its own subjects, and the instrument's answer over the real population is knowingly wrong by construction). ",
    "NOTHING LOOKS WRONG AT THE AUTHORING SITE, which is what separates this from ordinary bad data. The evidence is correct, the arm is correct, the annotation explaining why the rows are deliberately wrong is correct, and the author can defend every one of those facts individually. The defect is not the evidence but its HOME: it is the exact inverse of DESIGN section 4b's boundary, which locates an authorable invalid state in SOURCE HANDED TO THE COMPILER BY A FIXTURE. A fixture population is disposable and private to the check; an operational population is what the instrument testifies about. ",
    "THE MECHANISM THAT HIDES IT IS THE MISSING VERDICT, and this is the sharp part. The contamination is invisible exactly IN PROPORTION to how badly the instrument reports: an instrument that cannot refuse on its own uncertainty emits the honest per-row word -- UNOBSERVABLE -- into a report nobody adjudicates, and exits 0. So the report is truthful and the verdict is not, and no gate anywhere can see the difference. Strengthening the verdict is therefore what SURFACES the class rather than what fixes it, and a lane that adds the refusal without moving the evidence will simply start failing on its own fixtures. ",
    "THE DETECTOR IS A QUESTION ABOUT INTENT, ASKED STRUCTURALLY: does any row in the operational population have an EXPECTED verdict that is a refusal? If yes, the population is carrying evidence and the instrument's answer over it is not a measurement. It does not require reading the prose -- an annotation explaining that rows are deliberately wrong is itself the tell, because a correct operational row needs no such explanation. ",
    "SPECIMEN, gunbc#10454, and it is the reason this row exists. gunbc.namespace_cut_subject_roster carried two HostRustItemProbe rows citing src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs for build_import_adjacency and import_closure_from_adjacency, both of which had MOVED to src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/entry_resolve.rs. They were retained deliberately, with an annotation, as the discriminating RED for the stale-citation refusal arm in gunbc.namespace_cut_subject_observation host_probe_over_items -- an arm that is real and whose red is real. But gunbc.namespace_cut_subject_observation subject_roster_report wrote its report and returned ExitSuccess without ever inspecting whether any probe was Unobservable, so every pre-cut run of the cut's own exit-criterion instrument reported that it could not observe two of its subjects and exited 0. codex review 60319 named it. The repair was all three at once: correct the citations, move the RED to test.claim.namespace_cut_stale_citation_witness where host_probe_over_items was already parameterized on its item population for exactly that purpose, and make the command refuse on any Unobservable probe. ",
    "IT GENERALISES PAST INSTRUMENTS to any check whose regression probe lives in the population it polices -- a lint whose failing case is committed source, a migration census whose expecting-red subject is a live row, a conformance suite whose counterexample is an enrolled module. Wherever the check's denominator and its evidence are the same set, the check's answer over the real population is off by its own evidence, and the report cannot say so. ",
    "Rung found at 1: the harm was contained only because a reader adjudicated a report the command had already greened. Rung after gunbc#10454 is 2, mechanically preventable -- the command now refuses on any Unobservable probe, folded from the observation coproduct with no catch-all arm, so a new verdict variant fails to compile rather than defaulting to not-a-problem; but the invalid state is still WRITABLE and safety depends on that refusal executing and staying enrolled. CEILING 4, structural impossibility, and it is genuinely reachable because the distinction is decidable at construction: an operational subject roster and a fixture population are different kinds, and only one of them may carry a row whose expected verdict is a refusal. NEXT TRIGGER, capability and not artifact: a probe-population type distinguishing operationally-asserted subjects from fixture-authored ones, SUFFICIENT FOR a probe whose expected verdict is a refusal to have NO CONSTRUCTOR in an operational roster. The fixture file that discharged this specimen is not the trigger -- it relocated one instance and leaves the next roster equally able to accept evidence rows. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
